{"id":"sihon_2739","name":"Sihon","also":"","summary":"Striking down. The whole country on the east of Jordan, from the Arnon to the Jabbok, was possessed by the Amorites, whose king, Sihon, refused to permit the Israelites to pass through his territory, and put his army in array against them.","verses":34,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2,6]},{"id":"manasseh_1928","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[13,14]},{"id":"jair_708","name":"Jair","also":"","summary":"Was the son of Segub of the tribe of Judah – Segub being a son of Hezron who married a daughter of Machir.","verses":4,"father":"Segub","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"machir_1877","name":"Machir","also":"Machirites","summary":"Manasseh’s oldest son (Josh. 17:1), or probably his only son (see 1 Chr. 7:14, 15; comp. Num. 26:29-33; Josh. 13:31). His descendants are referred to under the name of Machirites, being the offspring of Gilead (Num. 26:29).","verses":17,"father":"Manasseh","mother":"Concubine the Aramitess","v":[15]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[18]},{"id":"joshua_1727","name":"Joshua","also":"Jehoshua, Oshea, Jesus, Jeshua, Hoshea","summary":"Jehovah is his help, or Jehovah the Saviour. The son of Nun, of the tribe of Ephraim, the successor of Moses as the leader of Israel.","verses":189,"father":"Nun","mother":"","v":[21,28]}],"places":[{"id":"bashan_159","name":"Bashan","kind":"Region","lat":32.80008,"lon":35.9373,"summary":"Light soil, first mentioned in Gen. 14:5, where it is said that Chedorlaomer and his confederates “smote the Rephaim in Ashteroth,” where Og the king of Bashan had his residence.","verses":52,"v":[1,3,4,10,11,13]},{"id":"edrei_358","name":"Edrei","kind":"City","lat":32.62414,"lon":36.099,"summary":"One of the chief towns of the kingdom of Bashan (Josh. 12:4, 5). Here Og was defeated by the Israelites, and the strength of the Amorites broken (Num. 21:33-35).","verses":8,"v":[1,10]},{"id":"heshbon_565","name":"Heshbon","kind":"City","lat":31.79819,"lon":35.80986,"summary":"Intelligence, a city ruled over by Sihon, king of the Amorites (Josh. 3:10; 13:17). It was taken by Moses (Num. 21:23-26), and became afterwards a Levitical city (Josh. 21:39) in the tribe of Reuben (Num. 32:37).","verses":37,"v":[2,6]},{"id":"argob_88","name":"Argob","kind":"Region","lat":33.144,"lon":36.136,"summary":"Stony heap, an “island,” as it has been called, of rock about 30 miles by 20, rising 20 or 30 feet above the table-land of Bashan; a region of crags and chasms wild and rugged in the extreme.","verses":4,"v":[4,13,14]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[8,17,20,25,27]},{"id":"mount_hermon_841","name":"mount Hermon","kind":"Mountain","lat":33.41611,"lon":35.8575,"summary":"","verses":7,"v":[8]},{"id":"river_of_arnon_1225","name":"river of Arnon","kind":"Water (River)","lat":31.4288,"lon":35.67701,"summary":"Swift, the southern boundary of the territory of Israel beyond Jordan, separating it from the land of Moab (Deut. 3:8, 16). This river (referred to twenty-four times in the Bible) rises in the mountains of Gilead, and after a circuitous course of about 80 miles through a deep ravine it falls into the Dead Sea nearly opposite Engedi.","verses":11,"v":[8,12,16]},{"id":"hermon_564","name":"Hermon","kind":"Mountain","lat":33.41611,"lon":35.8575,"summary":"A peak, the eastern prolongation of the Anti-Lebanon range, reaching to the height of about 9,200 feet above the Mediterranean. It marks the north boundary of Palestine (Deut. 3:8, 4:48; Josh. 11:3, 17; 13:11; 12:1), and is seen from a great distance.","verses":7,"v":[9]},{"id":"senir_1047","name":"Senir","kind":"","lat":33.41616,"lon":35.85726,"summary":"Shenir, the name given to Hermon by the Amorites (Deut. 3:9). It means “coat of mail” or “breastplate,” and is equivalent to “Sirion.” Some interpret the word as meaning “the prominent” or “the snowy mountain.”","verses":4,"v":[9]},{"id":"sirion_1101","name":"Sirion","kind":"","lat":33.41616,"lon":35.85726,"summary":"A breastplate, the Sidonian name of Hermon, Deut. 3:9; Ps. 29:6.","verses":3,"v":[9]},{"id":"gilead_475","name":"Gilead","kind":"Region","lat":32.75,"lon":35.75,"summary":"Hill of testimony, (Gen. 31:21), a mountainous region east of Jordan. From its mountainous character it is called “the mount of Gilead” (Gen. 31:25).","verses":80,"v":[10,12,13,15,16]},{"id":"salecah_1017","name":"Salecah","kind":"City","lat":32.49394,"lon":36.71034,"summary":"Wandering, a city of Bashan assigned to the half tribe of Manasseh (Deut. 3:10; Josh. 12:5; 13:11), identified with Salkhad, about 56 miles east of Jordan.","verses":4,"v":[10]},{"id":"rabbah_966","name":"Rabbah","kind":"","lat":31.95522,"lon":35.94503,"summary":"“Rabbath of the children of Ammon,” the chief city of the Ammonites, among the eastern hills, some 20 miles east of the Jordan, on the southern of the two streams which united with the Jabbok.","verses":14,"v":[11]},{"id":"aroer_93","name":"Aroer","kind":"City","lat":31.47151,"lon":35.82192,"summary":"A town on the north bank of the Arnon (Deut. 4:48; Judg. 11:26; 2 Kings 10:33), the southern boundary of the kingdom of Sihon (Josh. 12:2).","verses":9,"v":[12]},{"id":"gad_1286","name":"Gad","kind":"Region","lat":32.04697,"lon":35.7458,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1262 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":21,"v":[12,16]},{"id":"east-manasseh-half-tribe_1290","name":"East Manasseh (Half-Tribe)","kind":"Region","lat":32.64111,"lon":36.07154,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1268 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":14,"v":[13,14,15]},{"id":"rephaim_995","name":"Rephaim","kind":"","lat":32.80008,"lon":35.9373,"summary":"Lofty men; giants, (Gen. 14:5; 2 Sam. 21:16, 18, marg. A.V., Rapha, marg. R.V., Raphah; Deut. 3:13, R.V.; A.V., “giants”).","verses":1,"v":[13]},{"id":"havvoth-jair_535","name":"Havvoth-jair","kind":"","lat":32.04252,"lon":35.72424,"summary":"","verses":4,"v":[14]},{"id":"jabbok_609","name":"Jabbok","kind":"Water (River)","lat":32.19324,"lon":35.6763,"summary":"A pouring out, or a wrestling, one of the streams on the east of Jordan, into which it falls about midway between the Sea of Galilee and the Dead Sea, or about 45 miles below the Sea of Galilee.","verses":7,"v":[16]},{"id":"arabah_79","name":"Arabah","kind":"","lat":32.02968,"lon":35.52099,"summary":"Plain, in the Revised Version of 2 Kings 14:25; Josh. 3:16; 8:14; 2 Sam. 2:29; 4:7 (in all these passages the A.V. has “plain”); Amos 6:14 (A.V. “wilderness”).","verses":15,"v":[17]},{"id":"chinnereth_293","name":"Chinnereth","kind":"","lat":32.80678,"lon":35.58936,"summary":"Lyre, the singular form of the word (Deut. 3:17; Josh. 19:35), which is also used in the plural form, Chinneroth, the name of a fenced city which stood near the shore of the lake of Galilee, a little to the south of Tiberias.","verses":1,"v":[17]},{"id":"salt_sea_1021","name":"salt sea","kind":"Water","lat":31.57785,"lon":35.52394,"summary":"The name given by Greek writers of the second century to that inland sea called in Scripture the “salt sea” (Gen. 14:3; Num. 34:12), the “sea of the plain” (Deut. 3:17), the “east sea” (Ezek. 47:18; Joel 2:20), and simply “the sea” (Ezek. 47:8).","verses":9,"v":[17]},{"id":"lebanon_720","name":"Lebanon","kind":"Region","lat":33.92154,"lon":35.89897,"summary":"White, “the white mountain of Syria,” is the loftiest and most celebrated mountain range in Syria. It is a branch running southward from the Caucasus, and at its lower end forking into two parallel ranges, the eastern or Anti-Lebanon, and the western or Lebanon proper.","verses":56,"v":[25]},{"id":"pisgah_950","name":"Pisgah","kind":"","lat":31.76503,"lon":35.71857,"summary":"A part, a mountain summit in the land of Moab, in the territory of Reuben, where Balak offered up sacrifices (Num. 21:20; 23:14), and from which Moses viewed the promised land (Deut. 3:27).","verses":5,"v":[27]},{"id":"beth-peor_228","name":"Beth-peor","kind":"","lat":31.6561,"lon":35.71187,"summary":"House of Peor; i.e., “temple of Baal-peor”, a place in Moab, on the east of Jordan, opposite Jericho. It was in the tribe of Reuben (Josh. 13:20; Deut. 3:29; 4:46).","verses":4,"v":[29]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[6437,6437,6437,5927,5927,5927,1870,1870,1316,1316,5747,5747,4428,1316,1316,3605,3605,3605,5971,3318,3318,7122,7122,7122,4421,4421,154,154],[3068,3068,3068,559,413,413,408,408,3372,3372,3588,5414,5414,5414,853,3027,3027,3027,853,853,3605,5971,5971,776,776,776,6213,0,0,834,6213,6213,5511,5511,4428,567,567,567,834,3427,2809,2809],[3068,3068,3068,430,430,1571,5414,5747,4428,1316,1316,3605,3605,3605,5971,3027,3027,3027,5221,5221,5221,5221,1115,1115,8300,7604,7604],[1931,1931,6256,3920,3920,3605,8346,5892,5892,5892,3808,3808,3808,7151,7151,7151,3808,3808,3808,3947,3605,2256,709,709,4467,4467,5747,5747,1316,1316],[3605,428,5892,1219,1219,1364,1364,2346,1817,1817,1280,1280,905,905,905,7235,7235,6521,6521],[2763,2763,2763,2763,2763,834,6213,6213,6213,5511,5511,4428,2809,2809,2763,2763,4962,4962,802,2945,2945,3605,3605,5892],[3605,3605,929,929,7998,7998,5892,5892,5892,962,962,962,0,0],[1931,1931,6256,3947,3947,3027,8147,8147,4428,567,567,567,776,776,5676,3383,3383,769,769,769,5158,5704,2022,2022,2022,2